# TIER 1 FALLBACK - IDPP NEB with an inserted transition-state guess (ORCA 6.1)
# Use ONLY if OptTS-from-seed fails on two genuine attempts.
# Two documented ORCA 6.1 features are used here that the first-pass runs did not:
#   Interpolation IDPP : image-dependent pair potential path between endpoints,
#                        avoids the atom-overlap artifacts of linear interpolation.
#   TS "guessfile"     : the curated seed saddle is inserted into the path, so the
#                        band is built reactant -> seed -> product instead of
#                        blindly across the whole rearrangement.
# All three files (reactant.xyz, V-TSn_start.xyz, product.xyz) must share the
# same atom order (they do; all derive from the same molfiles).

! NEB-TS XTB2

%pal nprocs 3 end

%neb
  Product "product.xyz"        # the optimized product minimum of THIS step
  NImages 8
  Interpolation IDPP
  TS "V-TSn_start.xyz"         # curated seed saddle for THIS step
end

* xyzfile 0 1 reactant.xyz     # the optimized reactant minimum of THIS step

# After the run:
#   1) NEB-TS ends with an OptTS pass on the climbing image; check for exactly
#      ONE imaginary frequency in the frequency printout;
#   2) animate that mode; it must describe the reacting bond reorganization;
#   3) run t1_xTb_irc.inp from the converged saddle;
#   4) optimize both IRC endpoint geometries; they must land on the claimed
#      reactant and product minima;
#   5) only then record the barrier in the register as Verified.
